message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ECOCIDE: A Satellite-Based Evidentiary Framework for War-Time Environmental Crimes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Maske"
    given-names: "Sakshi D."
repository-code: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/ECOCIDE"
url: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/ECOCIDE"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for a Difference-in-Differences analysis of monthly
  Sentinel-2 NDVI after the destruction of Ukraine's Kakhovka Dam (6 June
  2023), comparing Kherson Oblast with four Romanian control counties
  (Tulcea, Galati, Braila, Constanta), with placebo tests, a quarterly event
  study, exact randomization inference and a control-only divergence check,
  alongside UNOSAT flood-extent layers. With cloud- and water-masked monthly
  composites and HAC inference on the monthly treated-minus-control gap,
  Kherson's NDVI declined relative to Tulcea by 0.108 (95% CI 0.007 to 0.209,
  p = 0.037; 0.069 with zone-specific seasonality, p = 0.005). Attribution to
  the dam is not established: Kherson ranks 2 of 5 in randomization
  inference and pre-event quarters deviate. Zenodo v1.0.0 and EarthArXiv
  preprint v1 report an earlier, superseded analysis.
keywords:
  - ecocide
  - remote sensing
  - causal inference
  - difference-in-differences
  - satellite evidence
  - Kakhovka Dam
  - NDVI
  - geospatial analysis
